    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "Amid the aftermath of one of the heaviest rainy seasons in three decades, reservoirs exceeded capacity and dam operations merged with seasonal rains to breach embankments, causing severe flooding. Turkey, as the upstream lever operator, initiated a diplomatic recalibration of water flow by agreeing to reduce releases, showcasing international cooperation as a transformative mechanism for flood mitigation.",
